From df50f5c5690a472d750a0e327ac4d05a4a9c8b79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:39:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: Add GCC CX power domain

The GCC GDSCs on SM8550 are backed by the RPMh CX power domain. Without
describing that parent domain, consumers of GCC-provided GDSCs can enable
their local domain without causing the required CX vote to be held.

Add the CX power-domain reference to the GCC node so votes from GCC GDSC
consumers can propagate to RPMh CX.

Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Abel Vesa <abel.vesa@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260924-qcom-tie-cx-to-gcc-v5-39-38732033e5b5@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

Upstream: linux-next commit df50f5c5690a472d750a0e327ac4d05a4a9c8b79 (next-20261009), applied by Bjorn Andersson.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
index bfb5dcfaa1..03f6d40ede 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -1194,6 +1194,7 @@
 				 <&ufs_mem_phy 1>,
 				 <&ufs_mem_phy 2>,
 				 <&usb_dp_qmpphy QMP_USB43DP_USB3_PIPE_CLK>;
+			power-domains = <&rpmhpd RPMHPD_CX>;
 		};
 
 		ipcc: mailbox@408000 {
